  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Solve each of the following equations by first putting the quadratic equation in standard form:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\frac1x+\\frac x4=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne0$. Multiply by $4x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4+x^2&=4x\\\\x^2-4x+4&=0\\\\(x-2)^2&=0\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\frac1{x-2}+\\frac1{x+1}=\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,\\ 5$",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne2,-1$. Multiply by $2(x-2)(x+1)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2(x+1)+2(x-2)&=(x-2)(x+1)\\\\4x-2&=x^2-x-2\\\\x^2-5x&=0\\\\x(x-5)&=0\\\\x&=0,\\ 5\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\frac1x-\\frac1{x+4}=\\frac13$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-6,\\ 2$",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne0,-4$. Multiply by $3x(x+4)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3(x+4)-3x&=x(x+4)\\\\12&=x^2+4x\\\\x^2+4x-12&=0\\\\(x+6)(x-2)&=0\\\\x&=-6,\\ 2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\frac5{2x}-\\frac x{x+1}=2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-\\frac56,\\ 1$\n\nClear denominators, then factorise.",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne0,-1$. Multiply by $2x(x+1)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}5(x+1)-2x^2&=4x(x+1)\\\\5x+5-2x^2&=4x^2+4x\\\\6x^2-x-5&=0\\\\(6x+5)(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=-\\frac56,\\ 1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{2x}{x+2}-\\frac1{2x-1}=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=0,\\ 3$\n\nClear denominators, then factorise.",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne-2,\\frac12$. Multiply by $(x+2)(2x-1)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2x(2x-1)-(x+2)&=(x+2)(2x-1)\\\\4x^2-3x-2&=2x^2+3x-2\\\\2x^2-6x&=0\\\\2x(x-3)&=0\\\\x&=0,\\ 3\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q7-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\frac{x+2}{x+1}-\\frac{x+3}{4x}=\\frac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=-3,\\ 1$\n\nClear denominators, then factorise.",
          "worked": "Here $x\\ne-1,0$. Multiply by $4x(x+1)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}4x(x+2)-(x+3)(x+1)&=2x(x+1)\\\\4x^2+8x-(x^2+4x+3)&=2x^2+2x\\\\3x^2+4x-3&=2x^2+2x\\\\x^2+2x-3&=0\\\\(x+3)(x-1)&=0\\\\x&=-3,\\ 1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      }
    ]
  },
